{"book":13,"chapter":29,"rubric":"PYTHON AS A FIRST LANGUAGE / METAPROGRAMMING / CHAPTER 29","slides":[{"title":"Decorators everywhere","sub":"Metaprogramming: start","short":"Decorators everywhere","main":"A decorator is the gentlest form of metaprogramming.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Functions","Methods and classes","Metaprogramming"],"captions":["A simple decorator takes a function and returns a wrapper, you know this already","In practice they are stacked, parameterized, applied to methods, classes, async functions","Decorators are the gentlest metaprogramming: code that works with code"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["@timed","def compute(x):","    return x * x"],"hl":[0],"lang":"python","size":12.0,"lh":26.0,"w":220.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":62.0,"y":50.0,"w":112.0,"h":26.0,"text":"functions","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":192.0,"y":50.0,"w":112.0,"h":26.0,"text":"methods","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":62.0,"y":90.0,"w":112.0,"h":26.0,"text":"classes","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b3","x":192.0,"y":90.0,"w":112.0,"h":26.0,"text":"async functions","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":308.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"@deco","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":268.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":256.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"decorators","tone":"green","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"metaclasses","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":270.0,"y":92.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"ast, dis","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":146.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":52.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":146.0,"y1":74.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":90.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[10.6,25.4]}]},{"title":"Order of application","sub":"Several decorators","short":"Order","main":"Applied bottom to top, read top to bottom.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Two decorators","Applied bottom to top","Read top to bottom"],"captions":["@bold over @italic over a function: two markup layers","italic wraps the function first, then bold wraps that: bold(italic(f))","On a call the top layer fires first; bold is outside: <b><i>text</i></b>"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":70.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["@bold","@italic","def text():","    return 'hello'"],"lang":"python","size":12.0,"lh":24.0,"w":220.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":170.0,"h":74.0,"text":"bold","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5,"dash":true,"o":0.5},{"t":"cell","id":"i","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":110.0,"h":44.0,"text":"italic","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5,"dash":true,"o":0.6},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":60.0,"h":24.0,"text":"text","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"w":200.0,"h":28.0,"text":"<b><i>hello</i></b>","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"applied bottom to top, read top to bottom","size":10.0}]],"cues":[11.2,25.7]}]},{"title":"With and without parentheses","sub":"func=None","short":"Parentheses","main":"The function is an optional first argument, settings by keyword only.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Two forms","func=None","A fork"],"captions":["We want both @repeat and @repeat(times=3): one decorator for both forms","First parameter is a function defaulting to None, settings are keyword-only","Got a function: wrap it now; not: return a real decorator that waits for it"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":70.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["@repeat","def hello(): ...","","@repeat(times=3)","def hello(): ..."],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":20.0,"w":220.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["def repeat(func=None, *, times=2):","    ...","# keyword-only settings"],"hl":[0],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["def repeat(func=None, *, times=2):","    def decorate(f):","        ...wrapper...","        return wrapper","    if func is not None:","        return decorate(func)","    return decorate"],"hl":[4,5,6],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[18.0,27.0]}]},{"title":"Methods","sub":"self and descriptors","short":"Methods","main":"@classmethod, @staticmethod, @property: always the topmost.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Ordinary method","Correct","Wrong"],"captions":["At definition a method is a plain function; self passes through the wrapper as the first argument","@classmethod, @staticmethod, @property create descriptors and go on top","The other way round, your wrapper gets a descriptor instead of a function and breaks"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["class Api:","    @logged","    def get(self, url):","        ...","# wrapper(self, url)"],"hl":[1],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["class Api:","    @classmethod","    @logged","    def make(cls): ..."],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":24.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":146.0,"text":"descriptor on top","tone":"green","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["class Api:","    @logged","    @classmethod","    def make(cls): ..."],"bad":[1,2],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":24.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":146.0,"text":"wrapper gets a classmethod object","tone":"red","size":10.0}]],"cues":[12.0,26.0]}]},{"title":"Class decorators","sub":"A class goes in","short":"Classes","main":"A class decorator receives the finished class.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["A class goes in","Registration","dataclass"],"captions":["A class decorator receives the finished class and returns it, modified or another","Common jobs: add to a registry, check attributes, add methods, replace with a singleton","@dataclass is a decorator that builds __init__, __repr__, __eq__ from annotations"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"class\nPlugin","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"@decorator","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":300.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"class\nPlugin'","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":112.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":134.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":226.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":258.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["PLUGINS = {}","","def plugin(cls):","    PLUGINS[cls.__name__] = cls","    return cls"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":30.0,"y":46.0,"lines":["@dataclass","class Point:","    x: int","    y: int"],"hl":[0],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":22.0,"w":220.0},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":295.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":70.0,"text":"__init__\n__repr__\n__eq__","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[9.4,27.4]}]},{"title":"functools.wraps","sub":"Keeping the function's face","short":"wraps","main":"wraps copies metadata and sets __wrapped__.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Without wraps","With wraps","__wrapped__"],"captions":["Without @wraps a wrapped function has another name and no docs: compute.__name__ == 'wrapper'","functools.wraps copies the name, docs, and module","And it sets __wrapped__ to the original, which inspect.signature follows to show real parameters"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["compute.__name__   # 'wrapper'","compute.__doc__    # None","help(compute)       # (*args, **kwargs)"],"bad":[0,1,2],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":290.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["@functools.wraps(func)","def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):","    ...","compute.__name__   # 'compute'"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":290.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"w","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"wrapper","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"original","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":142.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":218.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"text":"__wrapped__","size":10.0},{"t":"text","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"inspect.signature follows the link","tone":"green","size":10.0}]],"cues":[14.4,25.4]}]},{"title":"State","sub":"Attribute or class","short":"State","main":"A class decorator needs __get__ to work on methods.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Wrapper attribute","Class decorator","__get__ for methods"],"captions":["Simple state lives in the wrapper's own attribute: wrapper.calls += 1","With lots of state, use a class with __call__: the object stores data and is called like a function","An instance doesn't become a method itself: it needs __get__ from the descriptor protocol, as functions do"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["def counted(func):","    @wraps(func)","    def wrapper(*a, **kw):","        wrapper.calls += 1","        return func(*a, **kw)","    wrapper.calls = 0","    return wrapper"],"hl":[3,5],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["class CallCounter:","    def __init__(self, func):","        self.func = func","        self.calls = 0","    def __call__(self, *a, **kw):","        self.calls += 1","        return self.func(*a, **kw)"],"hl":[3,4,5],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["def __get__(self, obj, objtype=None):","    if obj is None:","        return self","    return types.MethodType(self, obj)"],"hl":[3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}]],"cues":[14.6,28.4]}]},{"title":"Async functions","sub":"A silent error","short":"async","main":"async def needs an async wrapper with await.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["A trap","Async wrapper","Universal"],"captions":["A plain wrapper gets a coroutine from an async function and never awaits it: timing and retries go wrong","An async def wrapper with await is needed: the result is awaited","A universal decorator picks a wrapper by inspect.iscoroutinefunction(func)"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["def timed(func):","    def wrapper(*a):","        start = time()","        result = func(*a)   # a coroutine!","        print(time() - start)"],"hl":[3],"bad":[3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["async def wrapper(*a):","    start = time()","    result = await func(*a)","    print(time() - start)","    return result"],"hl":[2],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["if inspect.iscoroutinefunction(func):","    return async_wrapper","return sync_wrapper"],"hl":[0],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}]],"cues":[14.5,28.4]}]},{"title":"Registering decorators","sub":"Routes and plugins","short":"Registration","main":"They fire at import and return the function as is.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Routes","Table","When it fires"],"captions":["The decorator takes an address and remembers the function: no wrapper, the function is returned as is","This is how web routes, event handlers, console commands, plugins, and tests work","Registration happens at definition, that is, at import; not imported means not registered"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["@route('/home')","def home(): ...","","@route('/about')","def about(): ..."],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":70.0,"text":"ROUTES","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"'/home' → home","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":90.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"'/about' → about","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":146.0,"y1":54.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":50.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":146.0,"y1":86.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":90.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"import app","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"table is filled","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":202.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"at definition, not at call","size":10.0}]],"cues":[14.7,27.3]}]},{"title":"In practice","sub":"retry, timed, lru_cache","short":"Practice","main":"Ten lines remove duplication from dozens of functions.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Reliability","Control","Speed"],"captions":["retry with a growing pause and timed: a few lines for dozens of functions","Permission checks, deprecation warnings (warnings.warn), argument checks from annotations","@lru_cache(maxsize=…) caches calls; cache_info() shows hits and misses"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":100.0,"y":56.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"@retry(times=3)","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":260.0,"y":56.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"@timed","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"retry on a temporary error · timing","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"@require_admin","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"@deprecated","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"@checked","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"permissions · warnings · types from annotations","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":40.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["@lru_cache(maxsize=256)","def fib(n): ...","fib.cache_info()","# hits=…, misses=…"],"hl":[0],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":280.0}]],"cues":[11.1,22.8]}]},{"title":"Types","sub":"ParamSpec","short":"Types","main":"Don't lose type hints on a decorated function.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Signature","ParamSpec","Why"],"captions":["For type checking, the wrapper must accept the same arguments as the original","typing has ParamSpec and Callable[P, R] for this: they describe another signature","Annotate library decorators so editors suggest parameters to users"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"f(x: int) → str","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"wrapper(*args, **kw)","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"hints lost","tone":"red","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["P = ParamSpec('P')","R = TypeVar('R')","def deco(f: Callable[P, R]) -> Callable[P, R]:","    ..."],"hl":[2],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"editor","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"sees f's parameters","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":202.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[10.4,24.0]}]},{"title":"Common mistakes","sub":"What not to do","short":"Mistakes","main":"Return the result and return the wrapper.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Result not returned","Wrapper not returned","Side effects"],"captions":["The wrapper doesn't return the original's result: functions now return None","The decorator doesn't return wrapper: the function's name now points to None","Code in the decorator body runs at import; and if logic isn't repeated, no decorator is needed"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["def wrapper(*a, **kw):","    func(*a, **kw)   # no return"],"bad":[1],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["def deco(func):","    def wrapper(*a): ...","    # forgot: return wrapper"],"bad":[2],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["def deco(func):","    print('loading!')   # at import","    return func"],"bad":[1],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[10.6,22.5]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"Decorators in depth","short":"Summary","main":"Order, parameters, wraps, state, async.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Order","Parameters","Methods and classes","State and async"],"captions":["Applied bottom to top, read top to bottom; @classmethod, @staticmethod, @property go on top","func=None and keyword-only settings: one form for both variants","A class decorator gets the finished class; always @wraps","State is a wrapper attribute or a class with __get__; async needs an async wrapper"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":56.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"@upper","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":96.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"@lower","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":76.0,"text":"bottom to top","tone":"green","size":11.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":66.0,"lines":["@repeat","@repeat(times=3)"],"lang":"python","size":12.5,"lh":28.0,"w":260.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"@wraps(func)","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":260.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"class decorator","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"__get__","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":260.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"async def wrapper","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.8,20.0,37.4]}]}]}